# Code style

- Write the smallest code that stays obvious.
- Comments only when the why is not visible in the code. No JSDoc. No comments in JSX.
- Pure shared functions go in `utils/`. Hooks sit next to the component that uses them.
- Do not add `lib/` for first-party code. Leave that name for a third-party wrapper later.
- Write nav and footer links in those components. Do not add a content module for them.

```tsx
// ❌ a folder of page copy for two links
export const mainNav = [{ href: "/projects", label: "Projects" }]

// ✅ the links live in the component that renders them
const links = [{ href: "/projects", label: "Projects" }] as const
```
